1.4.0 (2026-10-17)
- Organise your case: Move in list carries a tape up or down as you turn the left wheel; press to put it down.
- Sort the case A to Z, favourites to the top, or hidden to the bottom.
- ITEMS > MISC uses the same order (needs the updated CFW/52_RADIOMARU_MISC.JS and a reboot), with Holotape Case first.
- Making a tape a favourite no longer moves it; use Favourites to the top.
- Atomic Command and Grelok count as the Pip-Boy's own holotapes: the case leaves them out, Hide all never hides them, and ITEMS > MISC lists them first after the case.
- Holotapes whose icon is missing from the card show the Pip-Boy's own holotape picture (APPINFO/HOLO.IMG) instead of a drawn cassette.
- Options are grouped: Sort the case and Hide or show all open their own menus.

1.3.1 (2026-10-17)
- Holotapes now only play from the new Play holotape option. Pressing or holding the left wheel opens the options, so no stray press can start a game.

1.3.0 (2026-10-17)
- New option: Hide all custom holotapes. Hides every holotape installed from pip-boy.com, leaving only the Pip-Boy's own MISC items and the case.

1.2.1 (2026-10-17)
- Press the left wheel for the options and hold it to play, so a stray press no longer starts a holotape.

1.2.0 (2026-10-17)
- Now a submenu of ITEMS > MISC built on the Pip-Boy's own scrolling list, with the ITEMS header and tabs, instead of a separate full-screen app.
- Uses far less memory: only the .info file names are kept, and each tape's name and icon are read as its row comes on screen.
- Favourites show the filled box the Pip-Boy uses for equipped items. Hold the left wheel for the options.

1.1.0 (2026-10-12)
- Hides holotapes from ITEMS > MISC with a CFW patch instead of moving .info files, so pip-boy.com still sees every holotape.
- Changes show the next time ITEMS > MISC opens, without a reboot.
- "Store all others" is now "Hide all but favourites".
- Tapes stored by 1.0 are moved back into APPINFO and kept hidden.

